    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "True or False? Let $A$ and $B$ be sets in a universal set $U$.\n\n$A\\cap\\overline B=(A\\cup B)\\cap\\overline B$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "True.",
      "worked": "True. Intersecting $A\\cup B$ with $\\overline B$ removes every element in $B$, leaving exactly the elements of $A$ outside $B$. These form $A\\cap\\overline B$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
